# Full-Stack Feature Implementation Order

When a feature spans stacks, implement **one stack at a time** in this order. Never parallelize the same feature across stacks.

## Order

1. **Backend** (if `backend/` exists)
   - Define and implement API
   - Verify: `make test`
   - Write contract: `backend/.cursor/skills/add-feature/learned/<feature>.md`

2. **Web** (if `web/` exists) — **mandatory when the folder exists**
   - Consume the backend contract (do not invent endpoints)
   - Feature folder + page + route + sidebar
   - Verify: `npm run build`
   - Do not call the feature done after backend only

3. **App** (if `app/` exists)
   - Consume the same backend contract
   - Verify: `flutter analyze`

## Rules

- No parallelization of the same feature across stacks
- Backend contracts before web/app UI
- Each agent/subagent touches only one stack folder
- Verify before advancing
- Skip only stacks that are not present on disk

## Skill

Use `.cursor/skills/add-feature-fullstack/SKILL.md` to coordinate phases.
